from pathlib import Path
import hashlib,json
out=Path('research/frontier-44-special-representation-examples-28-six-step-owner-escalation-repairs/affine_bridge')
base=json.loads((out/'preimages.json').read_text()); helper='lem-finite-type-a-tensor-hecke-bars-and-complementary-coefficient-charts'
paths=['items/lem-type-a-tableau-central-summands-are-single-linkage-blocks.md','items/thm-parabolic-kl-polynomials-give-the-dual-canonical-transition-matrix.md']
for name in paths:
 p=Path(name);b=p.read_bytes(); assert hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()==base[name]; t=b.decode()
 if 'lem-type-a-tableau' in name:
  t=t.replace('deps: [lem-the-parabolic','deps: ['+helper+',\n       lem-the-parabolic',1)
  a=t.index('4.1 **The tensor/wedge bridge');z=t.index('\n\n4.2',a)
  t=t[:a]+r'''4.1 **The independent tensor/wedge bridge and opposite flag.** Apply [[lem-finite-type-a-tensor-hecke-bars-and-complementary-coefficient-charts]] before making any categorical identification. Its tensor generators act at $v=s^{-1}$, its positive chart transports to the sign module by $G_i=-H_i$ at $v=s$, and its complementary representative is $w_Kd(A)w_0$. The proved inverse tensor coefficient is $s^{\ell(w_C)-\ell(w_A)}P_{d(C)w_0,d(A)w_0}(s^{-2})$, so its value at $1$ is exactly the ordinary singular composition number in [F3]. The primitive ordinary-bar exterior embedding has coefficients $(-s)^{\ell(B,C)}$ on column permutations $C$ and sends the wedge $L_A$ to the ambient $L_{a(A)}$. Its signed inverse formula at $1$ therefore agrees term for term with finite Levi Weyl cancellation of the genuine generalized-standard character: $d_{A,B}(1)=[\Delta(B):L(A)]$. This uses character injectivity, and it keeps the equal-entry stabilizer separate from the column Levi. The helper proves the same transport for reversed factors; hence $\widetilde d_{B,A}(1)=[\bar\Delta(A):\bar L(B)]$. At $s=1$ the ordinary tensor bar matrix is the identity (each adjacent exchange has correction $s^{-1}-s=0$), so the reverse form of [F4] has monomial Gram matrix $I$. The identity $C(\widetilde L_A,T_B)=\delta_{AB}$ now says that the monomial coefficient matrix of $T$ is the transpose inverse of the coefficient matrix of $\widetilde L$, namely $\widetilde d^{\mathsf T}$. Thus the coefficient of $M(A)$ in $T_B$ at $1$ is $\widetilde d_{B,A}(1)=[\bar\Delta(A):\bar L(B)]=(X(B):\Delta(A))$ by step 3.1. All sign, longest-element and reverse-factor transports have been proved independently of this linkage conclusion. [F2, F3, F4, step 3.1, algebra]'''+t[z:]
 else:
  t=t.replace('deps:\n','deps:\n  - '+helper+'\n',1)
  a=t.index('1.2 **The polynomial identity');z=t.index('\n\n2.1',a)
  t=t[:a]+r'''1.2 **Explicit reciprocal action and signed chart.** The independent construction [[lem-finite-type-a-tensor-hecke-bars-and-complementary-coefficient-charts]] gives, at $v=s^{-1}$, the actual action $M_aH_i=M_{as_i}$ on an ascent, $sM_a$ on an equality, and $M_{as_i}+(s-s^{-1})M_a$ on a descent. The cyclic sorted tuple is fixed by the source bar and has stabilizer character $s$, so this is the trivial-induced tensor module with its induced bar, including equal entries. Changing generators to $G_i=-H_i$ gives the algebra at $v=s$, the sign character $-s$, and standard vector $n_{d(A)}=(-1)^{\ell(d(A))}M_A$. Thus the source-positive tensor fixed vector is the sign canonical vector multiplied by its leading sign. The helper's alternating-sum calculation and the inversion anti-involution of the Hecke algebra yield its coefficient $p_{A,B}(-s)$ and precisely the polynomial $p_{A,B}(s)$ stated. This resolves the bar sign by an explicit generator and standard-vector transport. [F1, F2, algebra]

1.3 **Ordinary-bar exterior embedding and complementary spherical chart.** The same helper constructs the primitive exterior vector of a decreasing column as $\sum_C(-s)^{\ell(B,C)}M_{a(C)}$. Its adjacent generator eigenvalue is $-s^{-1}$, quantum replacements preserve its coefficient-one normalization, and quasi-$R$ naturality identifies its ordinary bar with the wedge-factor bar. Product embeddings therefore have the displayed independent column sum, with leading coefficient one and positive-source corrections; triangular uniqueness gives $\iota(L_A)=L_{a(A)}$. Independently, the reverse-position chart has representative $c_A=w_Kd(A)w_0$. The actual bilinear normalization is $(M_a,\psi M_b^*)=\delta_{ab}$; symmetry and complementary positive/negative polynomial congruences give $U^{\mathsf T}\bar V=I$. Hence the inverse tensor chart is $D_{a,b}=\bar V_{b,a}=s^{\ell(w_b)-\ell(w_a)}P_{d(b)w_0,d(a)w_0}(s^{-2})$. Expanding the primitive exterior sum in this inverse chart proves the wedge inverse formula, including its signs and all repeated-entry indices. [F1, F2, F3, algebra]'''+t[z:]
  a=t.index('2.2 **The mixed composition');z=t.index('\n\n3.1',a)
  t=t[:a]+r'''2.2 **The mixed composition matrix.** Step 1.3 gives $D_{a(A),a(C)}(1)=P_{d(C)w_0,d(A)w_0}(1)$ and $d_{A,B}(1)=\sum_C(-1)^{\ell(B,C)}D_{a(A),a(C)}(1)$. The singular ordinary multiplicity theorem of [F3] has exactly these indices for the sorted-entry stabilizer. Finite Levi Weyl characters and PBW give $\mathrm{ch}\,M(B)=\sum_C(-1)^{\ell(B,C)}\mathrm{ch}\,M_{\mathrm{ord}}(C)$, with $C$ running over independent column permutations. Comparing coefficients of simple characters, which are linearly independent in the finite block, gives the same signed sum. Therefore $[M(B):L(A)]=d_{A,B}(1)$ with the displayed mixed parabolic matrix. The column subgroup and the equal-entry subgroup are used at separate stages, so repeated entries cause no conflation of sign and spherical families. [F2, F3, F4, step 1.3, algebra]'''+t[z:]
 assert p.read_bytes()==b
